# Offline, AI, And Security

## Offline-First

- Core practice, progress, navigation, and settings must work without network access.
- Seed content belongs in typed modules under `data/`; merge it with stored user progress instead of replacing user state.
- Guard `localStorage`, `window`, and `document` access with `import.meta.client` and `try/catch`.
- Treat corrupted or outdated browser storage as recoverable: fall back to defaults and keep the UI usable.

## AI Enhancements

- AI must never block completing a core practice flow.
- Server endpoints should accept validated input, return actionable user-safe errors, and avoid leaking provider details.
- Keep prompts, model calls, and provider-specific code isolated from UI and core scoring logic.
- If `OPENAI_API_KEY` is absent, return a graceful envelope response rather than crashing the app.

## Security

- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, keys, or credentials.
- Do not render unsanitized dynamic HTML. Prefer Vue text interpolation; sanitize imported HTML if it becomes necessary.
- Do not use `eval`, `new Function`, or dynamic code execution.
- Keep CSP changes intentional and narrow; document why any new external origin is required.
